# MONNI ads attribution (locked before spend)

Triad for every bi-weekly sprint: **Google Ads spend · Shopify order UTMs · PostHog funnel**.

## Environment

- Website: `https://teaandtonic.co.nz` (Shopify `tea-tonic-matakana.myshopify.com`)
- PostHog EU project `250395` (TeaAndTonic) via One `one_creds posthog` → `https://eu.posthog.com`
- Google Ads customer `4234565043` (display name still Tea & Tonic Matakana) via Make MCP `make-monni`
- Make connection `10474039` · Raw tool `s5966760_monni_google_ads_raw`

## Funnel event names (do not rename)

`$pageview` → `Product Viewed` → `Added to Cart` → `Checkout Started` → `Purchase`

- Theme: `snippets/posthog.liquid` + `assets/posthog-shopify.js`
- Purchase: Shopify Customer Events pixel `pixels/posthog-checkout.js` (must be installed in Admin)
- Autocapture is off. Do not add a second storefront PostHog pixel.

## Attribution

First-touch `utm_source`, `utm_medium`, `utm_campaign`, `utm_content`, `utm_term`, `gclid`, `gbraid`, `wbraid`, `landing_page`, `ph_distinct_id` are written to **cart attributes** so Shopify orders carry the same tags as PostHog.

Identify on **email** (not Shopify customer id) so checkout Purchase joins browse.

## Google Ads tracking templates (required on every campaign)

Search / Shopping final URL suffix:

`utm_source=google&utm_medium=cpc&utm_campaign={campaignid}&utm_content={adgroupid}&utm_term={keyword}`

PMax:

`utm_source=google&utm_medium=performance_max&utm_campaign={campaignid}`

Ignore Google’s self-reported conversions when they diverge from Shopify UTM revenue. Shopify landing_site + cart attributes are ground truth.
